WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:16.918
"Really? You have a mystery for us to solve?"

2
00:00:18.399 --> 00:00:20.040
Maggie asked Nathan eagerly.

3
00:00:20.921 --> 00:00:26.264
Henry stared at the five-dollar bill that Nathan had just slapped down on the lemonade stand.

4
00:00:27.005 --> 00:00:28.886
He felt a flutter of excitement.

5
00:00:28.906 --> 00:00:31.528
"Cool!" he said.

6
00:00:32.376 --> 00:00:33.197
"What's the mystery?"

7
00:00:33.497 --> 00:00:34.998
Cole sounded excited too.

8
00:00:35.018 --> 00:00:39.361
"It's about my little sister Nora," Nathan told them.

9
00:00:39.381 --> 00:00:41.522
"She's been acting weird lately."

10
00:00:43.063 --> 00:00:45.064
Henry's excited feeling faded.

11
00:00:45.885 --> 00:00:47.826
He traded a look with Maggie and Cole.

12
00:00:48.707 --> 00:00:50.028
Cole looked disappointed.

13
00:00:50.908 --> 00:00:52.349
Maggie rolled her eyes.

14
00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:55.091
"What's the mystery about that?"

15
00:00:55.451 --> 00:00:56.512
Maggie asked Nathan.

16
00:00:56.532 --> 00:01:00.555
"No offense, but Nora always acts kind of weird."

17
00:01:00.575 --> 00:01:03.345
"Yeah." Cole laughed.

18
00:01:04.286 --> 00:01:08.729
"Remember when she wore those pink pants every day for a week, and wanted everyone to call her

19
00:01:08.789 --> 00:01:10.090
Princess Pretty Pants?"

20
00:01:11.051 --> 00:01:13.093
"That's nothing," Maggie said.

21
00:01:13.113 --> 00:01:17.556
"What about the time she pretended she was an alien from outer space?"

22
00:01:18.517 --> 00:01:19.298
Henry nodded.

23
00:01:20.539 --> 00:01:26.123
Nora was only five years old, but she was famous in the neighborhood for doing strange stuff.

24
00:01:27.324 --> 00:01:31.348
"She argues with everybody about everything," Henry added.

25
00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:36.303
"And she's always dragging her stuffed animals around and pretending they're real."

26
00:01:37.204 --> 00:01:38.044
Nathan grinned.

27
00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:42.927
"She pretends her stuffed animals are real because she wants a pet so badly.

28
00:01:44.348 --> 00:01:48.611
She begged for a puppy for her fourth birthday, but Mom and Dad said no pets."

29
00:01:50.432 --> 00:01:53.935
"So it's no mystery that she's acting weird," Cole told Nathan again.

30
00:01:53.955 --> 00:01:56.116
Nathan shook his head.

31
00:01:56.136 --> 00:01:58.758
"This is different," he said.

32
00:01:58.778 --> 00:02:01.500
"Mom and Dad are really worried.

33
00:02:02.708 --> 00:02:04.650
They think Nora has been sleepwalking!

34
00:02:05.611 --> 00:02:09.134
They've caught her a couple of times walking around outside after dark."

35
00:02:10.795 --> 00:02:12.376
"Nora's been sleepwalking?"

36
00:02:12.697 --> 00:02:13.417
Henry said.

37
00:02:13.437 --> 00:02:18.281
"That sounds kind of serious, but it's not really a mystery."

38
00:02:19.242 --> 00:02:22.585
"I said they think she's been sleepwalking," Nathan said.

39
00:02:22.605 --> 00:02:24.627
"I think she's faking!"

40
00:02:24.647 --> 00:02:26.468
"Why do you think that?"

41
00:02:26.789 --> 00:02:27.429
Henry asked.

42
00:02:27.449 --> 00:02:30.672
"It's just a feeling," Nathan said.

43
00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.502
"I think she's up to something sneaky, but I'm not sure what it is."

44
00:02:36.303 --> 00:02:37.124
Maggie shrugged.

45
00:02:37.144 --> 00:02:38.644
"So what?

46
00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:42.026
Why do you care if she's pretending to sleepwalk?"

47
00:02:42.046 --> 00:02:46.069
"I just want to find out the truth," Nathan said.

48
00:02:46.089 --> 00:02:49.871
"Like I said, my parents are really worried about her.

49
00:02:51.131 --> 00:02:53.213
They're planning to take her to the doctor next week.

50
00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:56.755
If she's really sleepwalking, that's okay.

51
00:02:57.995 --> 00:03:01.289
But if she's faking it, she's making them worry for nothing!

52
00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:03.611
That's not fair."

53
00:03:04.672 --> 00:03:07.514
Henry still wasn't sure that this counted as a mystery.

54
00:03:08.474 --> 00:03:11.436
But Nathan was their friend, and he seemed pretty worried.

55
00:03:12.977 --> 00:03:18.181
Besides, investigating a mystery was better than sitting around pouring lemonade all day.

56
00:03:18.201 --> 00:03:21.943
"We can look into it, I guess," Henry said.

57
00:03:24.305 --> 00:03:26.126
Cole picked up the five-dollar bill.

58
00:03:26.146 --> 00:03:29.628
"But you should take this back for now," he told Nathan.

59
00:03:29.648 --> 00:03:32.149
"What are you doing, Cole?"

60
00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:33.270
Maggie cried.

61
00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:38.792
"This may not be much of a mystery, but that doesn't mean we'll solve it for free!"

62
00:03:38.812 --> 00:03:40.313
"I know."

63
00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:42.574
Cole gave the bill back to Nathan.

64
00:03:42.594 --> 00:03:46.135
"But The Lemonade Detectives have a guarantee, remember?"

65
00:03:47.356 --> 00:03:52.338
He pointed to the line on their sign that read "All Mysteries Solved, Guaranteed."

66
00:03:54.159 --> 00:03:55.019
Maggie looked at it.

67
00:03:55.039 --> 00:03:56.640
"So what?"

68
00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:57.420
she said.

69
00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:03.586
"A guarantee means Nathan only pays us when he's satisfied with our work," Cole replied.

70
00:04:03.606 --> 00:04:07.848
"That's what my dad always tells his customers, and he's a businessman."

71
00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:12.510
"Well, we're not businessmen," Maggie said with a frown.

72
00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:15.051
"We're just kids.

73
00:04:16.112 --> 00:04:18.333
And I need that money for my riding lessons!"

74
00:04:18.353 --> 00:04:22.374
"We'll get the money as soon as we solve the case," Cole said.

75
00:04:22.394 --> 00:04:25.796
"Cole has a point, Maggie," Henry said.

76
00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:29.282
"It doesn't make sense for Nathan to pay us now.

77
00:04:30.263 --> 00:04:33.345
If we can't solve the case, we'll just have to give the money back."

78
00:04:34.666 --> 00:04:36.247
Maggie still looked unhappy.

79
00:04:36.967 --> 00:04:37.768
But she nodded.

80
00:04:37.788 --> 00:04:40.369
"Fine," she said.

81
00:04:40.389 --> 00:04:44.752
"I guess it doesn't matter as long as we solve this case fast."

82
00:04:45.753 --> 00:04:48.495
Nathan tucked the five-dollar bill back into his pocket.

83
00:04:48.515 --> 00:04:51.577
"So does this mean you'll try to solve my mystery?"

84
00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:52.358
he asked.

85
00:04:53.999 --> 00:04:55.420
"Yes," Henry said.

86
00:04:56.316 --> 00:04:59.198
"The Lemonade Detectives are on the case!"

87
00:04:59.218 --> 00:05:03.060
"Let's go to your house and talk to Nora," Cole said.

88
00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:07.102
There were no customers waiting for lemonade just then.

89
00:05:08.082 --> 00:05:12.145
Maggie took out a small sign that said "Back in a While" and set it on the table.

90
00:05:13.105 --> 00:05:15.987
Then they all walked over to Nathan and Nora's house.

91
00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.051
you know where Nora is right now?"

92
00:05:24.471 --> 00:05:25.452
Maggie asked Nathan.

93
00:05:26.976 --> 00:05:29.557
"She's probably in the playroom," Nathan said.

94
00:05:29.577 --> 00:05:33.059
"It's at the back of the house so we can go in the back door."

95
00:05:34.699 --> 00:05:36.760
He led the way around the side of the house.

96
00:05:37.741 --> 00:05:40.922
They turned the corner just in time to see a window slide open.

97
00:05:40.942 --> 00:05:45.784
A second later Nora climbed out and tiptoed across the backyard!
